              "text": "ārdor, ārdōris — \"burning heat; passion\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ārdor flammārum mūrōs nigrōs fēcit. The heat of the flames blackened the walls."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine, 3rd declension, from ārdeō, 'to burn' (taught). Also a burning eagerness. English ardour."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ārdor is built on ārdeō, \"to burn\" (EtymDB): burning, in fire and in feeling. English ardour comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
